Three heap holders give their memory back (measured on OoT, 2026-11-10: 1,735 MiB live in play):
the texture cache's upload scratch buffers are freed every 256 frames when over 8 MiB and the ASTC
scan buffer after a scan over 8 MiB (64 + 56 MiB were kept from the save load on); a shader IR
pool keeps at most 4 MiB between shaders (113 MiB were kept in six pools); the descriptor update
queues start at an eighth of their size and grow when a frame needs more (120 MiB were held).

